#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115078 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115249 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b7f42188-bf51-5546-89fb-e33ba47c4b5e" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Row Operations Required To Find the Inverse of a 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "7c480d6a-93a1-56ec-a75c-56402e872c92" :question/math-academy-id "e-4723" :question/problem "The inverse of the matrix $A$ is found using row operations, as shown below. What are the row operations corresponding to each step?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,I\\,] & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 6 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & \\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2} & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We write down $A$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply the standard Gauss-Jordan method to transform the matrix $A$ into the identity matrix. We perform the same row operations on both matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,I\\,] & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 6 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & \\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-3){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2} & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding row operations are\n\n$$\nR_1 := \\dfrac{1}{2}R_1,\n\\qquad\nR_1 := R_1+(-3)R_2.\n$$\n\nThe matrix $A^{-1}$ is given by the right-hand side of our big matrix after all of the transformations have been completed. Therefore, \n![](images/b3/b34f8d0d2c5f05f6c104395e75e9f5c93df7812155e09bc47828747e752d003a.svg)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115079 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115250 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8a4b135f-df0d-5443-bb93-796f32c380c6" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Inverse of a 2x2 Matrix Calculated Using Row Operations"}] :question/id #uuid "e13311fb-21de-58d4-aed0-18304b48bb0c" :question/math-academy-id "e-4724" :question/problem "The inverse of the $2\\times 2$ matrix $A$ is found using row operations, as shown below. Complete the process, and determine $A^{-1}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,I\\,] & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=\\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 &  &  \\\\ 0 & 1 &  & \\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We write down $A$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply the standard Gauss-Jordan method to transform the matrix $A$ into the identity matrix. We perform the same row operations on both matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,I\\,] & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe matrix $A^{-1}$ is given by the right-hand side of our big matrix after all of the transformations have been completed. Therefore, \n![](images/91/919674aa42fd55c536318518d9e14de07a515d3c33cb7868378ce168221f13ff.svg)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115080 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115251 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "77d78574-a17c-5fc3-8c14-3aaec7753b3c" :knowledge-point/title "Transforming a 2x2 Matrix Into the Identity Matrix Using Row Operations"}] :question/id #uuid "ff4b4389-d8ff-5b48-904b-ff405abb4e48" :question/math-academy-id "e-4725" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are transformed into the $2\\times 2$ identity matrix after applying the row operations $R_1 \\leftrightarrow R_2 \\,$ and $\\, R_2 :=  R_2+(-1)R_1?$\n\n![](images/e0/e034f65af225ce46015a5accae774a24eed8617590a583a2a885b4b1c5332103.svg)" :question/worked-solution "Let's apply the operations to each of the matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne I\\,\\times  \\\\ B & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =I\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$B$ only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266081 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115250 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8a4b135f-df0d-5443-bb93-796f32c380c6" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Inverse of a 2x2 Matrix Calculated Using Row Operations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c5e09aa-a71a-5bc1-abdb-ffbee8ae45ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{A}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263934} {:answer/id #uuid "7b00896b-7411-5bea-b442-6e238235690f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{A}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264066} {:answer/id #uuid "7c1c69e8-11c6-5242-a605-cf735a7f46aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{A}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264072} {:answer/id #uuid "967a322b-3f8a-5022-9edc-92691060c3ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{A}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264286} {:answer/id #uuid "ee11f2f0-386f-5dd5-b7b7-a51ec3fc0b57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{A}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3} & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265080}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7b00896b-7411-5bea-b442-6e238235690f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{A}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264066} :answer-field/id #uuid "10fa802d-e4cb-5576-8c4b-61c19f125b76" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265274}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9e343a4f-de97-54f0-9ea2-a4b90179e66c" :question/math-academy-id "q-131380" :question/problem "The inverse of the $2\\times 2$ matrix $A$ is found using row operations, as shown below. Complete the process, and determine ${A}^{-1}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,I\\,] & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :=\\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & \\bbox[2pt,lightgray]{\\phantom{a}} & \\bbox[2pt,lightgray]{\\phantom{a}} \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\bbox[2pt,lightgray]{\\phantom{a}} & \\bbox[2pt,lightgray]{\\phantom{a}}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We write down $A$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply the standard Gauss-Jordan method to transform the matrix $A$ into the identity matrix. We perform the same row operations on both matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,I\\,] & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :=(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe matrix ${A}^{-1}$ is given by the right-hand side of our big matrix after all of the transformations have been completed. Therefore, \n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186367380 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115250 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8a4b135f-df0d-5443-bb93-796f32c380c6" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Inverse of a 2x2 Matrix Calculated Using Row Operations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e5e4d4a6-47d4-594a-bb6e-b1ace8a4a6c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{U}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367382} {:answer/id #uuid "881a37c9-d7f8-59f2-b7ee-095fc504a064" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{U}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367383} {:answer/id #uuid "4be5e6c7-dd16-573c-b14b-40d745a1e82f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{U}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367384} {:answer/id #uuid "8b9dbd30-b95e-598f-816b-01942329f555" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{U}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367385} {:answer/id #uuid "ff56a692-b286-52a3-8b6e-59978067c457" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{U}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367386}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b9dbd30-b95e-598f-816b-01942329f555" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{U}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367385} :answer-field/id #uuid "70d91655-25da-5fba-9d38-73eb64f27906" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367381}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2d8a7a16-61ab-5f35-8a80-89b943b1ed70" :question/math-academy-id "q-131385" :question/problem "The inverse of the $2\\times 2$ matrix $U$ is found using row operations, as shown below. Complete the process, and determine ${U}^{-1}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[U\\,|\\,I\\,] & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=\\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 &  &  \\\\ 0 & 1 &  & \\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We write down $U$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply the standard Gauss-Jordan method to transform the matrix $U$ into the identity matrix. We perform the same row operations on both matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[U\\,|\\,I\\,] & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-4){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe matrix ${U}^{-1}$ is given by the right-hand side of our big matrix after all of the transformations have been completed. Therefore, \n\n$$\n{U}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383286 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115249 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b7f42188-bf51-5546-89fb-e33ba47c4b5e" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Row Operations Required To Find the Inverse of a 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b273511-a7cc-5c6a-9dd8-0abe26274e77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383288} {:answer/id #uuid "90009beb-fdae-54f4-a1be-b67a0e2f37d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}↔{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383289} {:answer/id #uuid "d949a385-01a3-547e-bde2-e99e2407774c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383290} {:answer/id #uuid "f51e7881-94f1-58ab-ab06-c8b6f7294763" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:=-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383291} {:answer/id #uuid "32471165-41bc-5064-a412-16c9c2cff15b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}↔{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383292}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "32471165-41bc-5064-a412-16c9c2cff15b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}↔{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383292} :answer-field/id #uuid "177d43b0-3c90-586e-81e2-8ae60e0195aa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383287}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c0502d3a-1260-56b0-b010-809a7a1a12de" :question/math-academy-id "q-131980" :question/problem "The inverse of the matrix $A$ is found using row operations, as shown below. What are the row operations corresponding to each step?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,I] & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We write down $A$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply the standard Gauss-Jordan method to transform the matrix $A$ into the identity matrix. We perform the same row operations on both matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,I] & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding row operations are\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}↔{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1}.\n$$\n\nThe matrix ${A}^{-1}$ is given by the right-hand side of our big matrix after all of the transformations have been completed. Therefore, \n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186398375 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115249 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b7f42188-bf51-5546-89fb-e33ba47c4b5e" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Row Operations Required To Find the Inverse of a 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "92b6e22e-e14f-536e-a8cf-ab5edfb0d027" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398377} {:answer/id #uuid "3f468114-a837-5315-9463-743e098f65ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398378} {:answer/id #uuid "3540d783-48ba-526c-a122-0ebe4bb9b9be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398379} {:answer/id #uuid "dd01665e-3643-581b-8e10-6bc426a9baba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398380} {:answer/id #uuid "8a98a201-ff8f-5c9f-a6de-5a59d7503724" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+3{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398381}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3540d783-48ba-526c-a122-0ebe4bb9b9be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398379} :answer-field/id #uuid "89863539-4901-5ced-a4bc-1a69933efb51" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398376}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "41dc19c4-f697-52b3-b9b5-76ded5157f14" :question/math-academy-id "q-131999" :question/problem "The inverse of the matrix $Y$ is found using row operations, as shown below. What are the row operations corresponding to each step?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[Y\\,|\\,I] & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We write down $Y$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply the standard Gauss-Jordan method to transform the matrix $Y$ into the identity matrix. We perform the same row operations on both matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[Y\\,|\\,I\\,] & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding row operations are\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1}.\n$$\n\nThe matrix ${Y}^{-1}$ is given by the right-hand side of our big matrix after all of the transformations have been completed. Therefore, \n\n$$\n{Y}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186401995 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115249 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b7f42188-bf51-5546-89fb-e33ba47c4b5e" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Row Operations Required To Find the Inverse of a 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f4eea07e-f2f3-5991-9f8c-d1a3d485cb8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+4{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401997} {:answer/id #uuid "b42745fe-be44-51aa-b6af-8f31a15a57a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1},\\,{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+\\frac{3}{4}{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401998} {:answer/id #uuid "428db092-3f21-5636-9fa7-75f2fd6123d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1},\\,{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-3){R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401999} {:answer/id #uuid "8f69e7f4-02bf-5a3c-99ee-ec0db4ec6abb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402000} {:answer/id #uuid "3e91bc4e-4104-5e61-9a68-1d8607d11d41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+\\frac{4}{3}{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402001}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e91bc4e-4104-5e61-9a68-1d8607d11d41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+\\frac{4}{3}{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402001} :answer-field/id #uuid "b2cc2c12-ff60-5e41-a718-fde30b82b390" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401996}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d8e64088-2308-5369-8285-5d893b0dfcdf" :question/math-academy-id "q-31945" :question/problem "The inverse of the matrix $K$ is found using row operations, as shown below. What are the row operations corresponding to the blank spaces?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[K\\,|\\,I] & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=-\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -\\frac{4}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3} & 0 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -\\frac{4}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{3} & -\\frac{2}{3} & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :=3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -\\frac{4}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 3\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We write down $K$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply the standard Gauss-Jordan method to transform the matrix $K$ into the identity matrix. We perform the same row operations on both matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[K\\,|\\,I] & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=-\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -\\frac{4}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3} & 0 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -\\frac{4}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{3} & -\\frac{2}{3} & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :=3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -\\frac{4}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 3\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+\\frac{4}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding row operations are\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}:=-\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{2}:=3{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+\\frac{4}{3}{R}_{2}.\n$$\n\nThe matrix ${K}^{-1}$ is given by the right-hand side of our big matrix after all of the transformations have been completed. Therefore, \n\n$$\n{K}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299766 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115249 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b7f42188-bf51-5546-89fb-e33ba47c4b5e" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Row Operations Required To Find the Inverse of a 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "199ad44b-08ae-5e76-b788-13464d63a1ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1},\\,{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297662} {:answer/id #uuid "2ac5438a-8e7b-5dde-ab88-1b32e6237f7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1},\\,{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297730} {:answer/id #uuid "371fb1fe-9e49-5767-95a0-1b19d5009c9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1},\\,{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297775} {:answer/id #uuid "89c1f359-0e3f-54ae-984d-a8691fc6e15b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298149} {:answer/id #uuid "9a39d6c1-84df-5033-981a-30675ce233c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1},\\,{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298222}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2ac5438a-8e7b-5dde-ab88-1b32e6237f7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1},\\,{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297730} :answer-field/id #uuid "a3afd797-ff75-5529-8d43-2b2e29e4507c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299184}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9a2668c7-61c5-574f-ad15-7bac1011df33" :question/math-academy-id "q-31946" :question/problem "The inverse of the matrix $U$ is found using row operations, as shown below. What are the row operations corresponding to each step?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[U\\,|\\,I] & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We write down $U$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply the standard Gauss-Jordan method to transform the matrix $U$ into the identity matrix. We perform the same row operations on both matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[U\\,|\\,I] & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding row operations are\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1},\\,{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{2}.\n$$\n\nThe matrix ${U}^{-1}$ is given by the right-hand side of our big matrix after all of the transformations have been completed. Therefore, \n\n$$\n{U}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115852 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115251 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "77d78574-a17c-5fc3-8c14-3aaec7753b3c" :knowledge-point/title "Transforming a 2x2 Matrix Into the Identity Matrix Using Row Operations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7d1574dd-091a-52ae-8eb0-535fd3914634" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460005} {:answer/id #uuid "7586863f-229d-578d-ac84-f0e761139eda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460006}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7d1574dd-091a-52ae-8eb0-535fd3914634" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460005} :answer-field/id #uuid "bec46523-5df6-5a30-a264-03c885caa2bd" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460869} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ed431171-2bbf-5c8c-afad-a46ecfc1b548" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460007} {:answer/id #uuid "8cfdbbbb-5343-5c70-85ff-8ea0242e36fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460008}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8cfdbbbb-5343-5c70-85ff-8ea0242e36fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460008} :answer-field/id #uuid "e90e3cb2-cf8d-5f7e-8a1d-7e3fced79e84" :answer-field/key "B" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460870} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "849f41f5-f501-53ee-8ecc-b0fca7647ab4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460009} {:answer/id #uuid "b44c80de-5afb-5ae0-9c0e-9042718b52cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460010}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "849f41f5-f501-53ee-8ecc-b0fca7647ab4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460009} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b060f26-347b-584a-9045-d8d27b9e7501" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460871}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "90c835e0-83aa-519b-9995-715569dd5d93" :question/math-academy-id "q-43000" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are transformed into the $2\\times 2$ identity matrix after applying the row operations ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{1}:=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1}?$\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's apply the operations to each of the matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne I\\,\\times  \\\\ B & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =I\\,✓ \\\\ C & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne I\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$B$ only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329705 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115250 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8a4b135f-df0d-5443-bb93-796f32c380c6" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Inverse of a 2x2 Matrix Calculated Using Row Operations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e1b6e1f-40a5-5d7b-8784-52be2d4ca406" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{Q}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327051} {:answer/id #uuid "2b0757fc-669d-5a05-92ec-a08c787dfe41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{Q}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327315} {:answer/id #uuid "e14f5ab4-adf3-5429-9343-5b19271d44db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{Q}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328904} {:answer/id #uuid "efa73263-ce8a-5673-93de-df606171424a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{Q}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329027} {:answer/id #uuid "f1bdcfc9-f2d4-5cb8-871e-d5337b9f43b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{Q}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329043}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "efa73263-ce8a-5673-93de-df606171424a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{Q}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329027} :answer-field/id #uuid "2268f6a5-26ee-5dac-8ee4-d4c7d3159727" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329245}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ce5531aa-6b05-5b32-a6bf-6f89f79abdc1" :question/math-academy-id "q-43005" :question/problem "The inverse of the $2\\times 2$ matrix $Q$ is found using row operations, as shown below. Complete the process, and determine ${Q}^{-1}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[Q\\,|\\,I\\,] & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & \\,4 & \\,1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\,-1 & \\,-1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :=(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=\\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 &  &  \\\\ 0 & 1 &  & \\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We write down $Q$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply the standard Gauss-Jordan method to transform the matrix $Q$ into the identity matrix. We perform the same row operations on both matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[Q\\,|\\,I\\,] & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & \\,4 & \\,1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\,-1 & \\,-1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :=(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-4){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe matrix ${Q}^{-1}$ is given by the right-hand side of our big matrix after all of the transformations have been completed. Therefore, \n\n$$\n{Q}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345092 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115251 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "77d78574-a17c-5fc3-8c14-3aaec7753b3c" :knowledge-point/title "Transforming a 2x2 Matrix Into the Identity Matrix Using Row Operations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85e64603-bb6e-5b0f-a72d-80a8ccc3450d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468118} {:answer/id #uuid "bb5f4f63-4be8-5a5b-b8cd-fa7559af4fa1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468119}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "85e64603-bb6e-5b0f-a72d-80a8ccc3450d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468118} :answer-field/id #uuid "c1db1d1e-60e6-5396-8aa1-ee91b508535f" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468780} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e2a0153d-23de-5108-888f-f2b222f9131f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468120} {:answer/id #uuid "9cd47bee-3079-5cc3-a48e-29d195deb027" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468121}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9cd47bee-3079-5cc3-a48e-29d195deb027" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468121} :answer-field/id #uuid "e4c80179-cb50-56e3-9723-38b39e5ea82c" :answer-field/key "B" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468781} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "83fa1bed-27f2-56b2-bedb-00ae85826918" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468122} {:answer/id #uuid "58093b55-be97-532c-ab81-3f3b5e4b6b65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468123}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "83fa1bed-27f2-56b2-bedb-00ae85826918" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468122} :answer-field/id #uuid "046de83c-fd46-54bf-b6be-3214402a6cb6" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468782}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "21485ec9-747a-5129-ba2c-794c570827bf" :question/math-academy-id "q-75496" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are transformed into the $2\\times 2$ identity matrix after applying the row operations ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1}?$\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's apply the operations to each of the matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -3 \\\\ 4 & 13\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne I\\,\\times  \\\\ B & =\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =I\\,✓ \\\\ C & =\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne I\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$B$ only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345095 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115251 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "77d78574-a17c-5fc3-8c14-3aaec7753b3c" :knowledge-point/title "Transforming a 2x2 Matrix Into the Identity Matrix Using Row Operations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eaf41b36-30bd-512a-957e-7a79e4183513" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468124} {:answer/id #uuid "9454a215-809e-5191-9a6a-ef7b9461b589" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468125}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eaf41b36-30bd-512a-957e-7a79e4183513" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 